    <item>
      <title>Why we stopped buying on the spot market</title>
      <link>https://harborline.example.com/why-we-stopped-buying-spot/</link>
      <dc:creator><![CDATA[mara]]></dc:creator>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p>For three years we bought whatever scored well and was available. It made for an interesting menu and a miserable supply chain.</p>
<p>Repeat contracts cost more per kilo and less per year, because we stopped paying for the cost of switching: new profiles, new packaging, new conversations with nineteen cafes.</p>
<blockquote><p>The cheapest lot is the one you already know how to roast.</p></blockquote>
      ]]></content:encoded>
      <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Repeat contracts cost more per kilo and less per year.]]></excerpt:encoded>
